rius of sodium-deprived rats</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><year>1988</year><volume>406</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>410</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3254418</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nakamura</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Norgren</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sodium-deficient diet reduces gustatory activity in the nucleus of the solitary tract of behaving rats</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1995</year><volume>269</volume><fpage>R647</fpage><lpage>661</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7573568</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dietary sodium deprivation reduces gustatory neural responses of the parabrachial nucleus in rats</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>2008</year><volume>432</volume><fpage>170</fpage><lpage>173</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18255225</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neulet.2007.10.034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bernstein</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hennessy</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Amiloride-sensitive sodium channels and expression of sodium appetite in rats</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1987</year><volume>253</volume><fpage>R371</fpage><lpage>374</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2441613</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lindemann</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name>